Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  31 AUG 94 at 18 19 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  90    AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  COMEDO TYPE  10     SEE NOTE   NOTE  Tumor diameter measures at least 2 0cm  Multiple inked resection margins are positive for carcinoma  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 58                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked  and sectioned to reveal a 2 0cm nodule with multilobulated surface and areas of friable tan tissue admixed with firm white tissue  Representative sections frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remaining tissue submitted entirely in A through M  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED INVASIVE CARCINOMA O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Nash  Jennifer Reports To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Left breast carcinoma  Two satellite nodules by MRI inferior and anterior to main mass  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH AREAS OF SPINDLE CELL CARCINOMA  METAPLASTIC CARCINOMA   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  4  SEE NOTE AND TABLE  1  NOTE  The spindle cell component demonstrates greater cellularity  mitotic activity  and pleomorphism than that typically seen in reactive stroma  The spindle cells are focally positive for cytokeratin AEI 3  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  2 and show focal  weak staining for wide spectrum cytokeratin  they are largely negative for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   These findings are consistent with the diagnosis of a spindle cell carcinoma component  The tumor cells are negative for GCDFP 15 and nuclear WT 1  The latter result  in conjunction with the presence of an in situ component  supports a breast origin for this tumor  All three nodules show a similar histology  A prominent  dense lymphocytic response is present  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  Three nodules   REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm Grade  3 Lymphatic vessel invasion  Present  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within and beyond the region of the mass  Grade of the ductal carcinoma in situ  3 Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for receptors  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   LYMPH NODES  SENTINEL  SUPERIOR TO LEFT BREAST   EXCISION  RARE ISOLATED TUMOR CELLS PRESENT IN 1 OF 4 LYMPH NODES  SEE TABLE  2  TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS  2 SENTINEL LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  1 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  4 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   0 Method of detection  Cytokeratin immunohistochemistry Extracapsular extension  None Other forms of axillary involvement  None GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lump  short superior  long lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan yellow fibrofatty breast excision specimen  There is a short stitch designating superior and a long lateral  The posterior aspect is inked black  the anterior blue  the superior green  and the inferior yellow  On sectioning  three separate masses are identified  The largest superior mass measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm and is ill defined  tan pink and focally hemorrhagic  coming to 0 4cm from the posterior  1 0cm from the medial  1 2cm from the superior  1 4cm from the anterior  1 6cm from the lateral  and 3 1cm from the inferior margins  Located 1 5cm inferior is another ill defined  tan pink and focally hemorrhagic  indurated mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  This mass is 0 5cm from the posterior  0 8cm from the medial  1 2cm from both the anterior and the lateral  1 0cm from the inferior and 4 6cm from the superior margins  The third indurated  ill defined mass is located at the anterolateral aspect  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  It is 0 5cm from the anterior  0 6cm from the lateral  0 8cm from the posterior  1 5cm from the superior  2 8cm from the medial  and 4 5cm from the inferior margins  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma consists of tan white fibrotic tissue and yellow  focally hemorrhagic and lobulated fat  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The entire superior mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The entire inferior mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The entire anterolateral mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Intervening parenchyma between the superior and the inferior mass with the aspect closest to the superior mass inked orange  not a margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved parenchyma  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lymph node  suspicious    are REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm in aggregate of yellow  lobulated fat which contains four potential lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Rebecca J DiIorio  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Jennifer Nash  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s ac