he predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a breast biopsy containing a 1 1cm in greatest diameter stellate  firm  tan mass approaching an inked margin  Representative tissue is frozen as frozen section  1  and submitted in A  remainder of mass in B through D with representative surrounding in E through G  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND CRIBRIFORM DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  PRESENT AT AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
