kable skin with an unremarkable 3 0cm nipple  The specimen is oriented by a short suture designating the superior and long suture designating the lateral margins  Attached is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm axillary tail  The specimen is black inked and serially sectioned to reveal a medially located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm cavitary lesion lined by tan pink smooth membranous tissue and surrounded by fat necrosis with blue injected dye  This lesion abuts all the inked margins  The remainder of parenchyma is remarkable for very firm rubbery white fibrous tissue extending to all inked margins  The axillary tail is serially sectioned to reveal multiple nodes and white fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted  SECTION CODE  D  deep and superior E  deep and medial F  cavity medial and inferior G  anterior portion of fibrous tissue adjacent to cavity and superior H  anterior inferior fibrous tissue I  deep central J  lateral and deep K  medial and superior L  medial and inferior M  central and anterior N  central and deep O  one lymph node bisected P  multiple lymph nodes Q  fibrous tissue R  O 5cm nodule within fibrous tissue  W  cavity  deep lateral X JJ  additional sections near biopsy site  Labelled  additional right axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm unoriented tan yellow fibrofatty portion of breast serially sectioned and submitted entirely as S T  Resident  SOHEIL DADRAS  MD  PHD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 LYMPH NODE  RIGHT SENTINEL   REMOVED_CASE_ID    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2 LYMPH NODE  RIGHT SENTINEL  476   RARE ATYPICAL CELLS IN SINUS  DIFFER TO PERMANENT SECTIONS  DISCUSSED WITH DR  SMITH  O R  Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Y