th this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of fibroadipose tissue which is oriented with two short sutures where the superior aspect  two long sutures for the medial  and one long and one short for anterior  There is a needle localization wire and accompanying specimen radiograph  The entire specimen is inked black while the anterior surface is double inked yellow  medial blue  and posterior green  The specimen is sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a 0 3cm in diameter firm gray stellate area  too small to freeze  The specimen is submitted in its entirety from superior to inferior in cassettes A through F  with the lesion in cassette B   D  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST MASS  SUSPICIOUS LESION    CARCINOMA    RADIAL SCAR  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
