Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 MAY 96 ACCESSIONED ON  07 MAY 96 at 13 14 CLINICAL DATA  New 1 0cm suspicious mass on mammography on May 3rd  Fine needle aspirate on May 6th was suspicious  Undergoing lumpectomy and axillary section                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  SPECIMEN  1   BIOPSY  TUBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE SUPERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  BREAST  RIGHT  SPECIMEN  2   BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  SPECIMEN  3   BIOPSY  FAT AND SCANT UNREMARKABLE GLANDULAR TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN EIGHTEEN OF EIGHTEEN LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 MAY 96 at 13 43                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 MAY 96 at 16 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of breast with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined stellate  firm mass approximately 1 0cm in greatest dimension  adjacent to the superior medial inked margin  A representative section of this area is frozen as FX 1  and saved frozen  Representative sections of the medial half are submitted from superior to inferior  A through E  and representative sections of the lateral half are submitted superior to inferior in F through J  Labeled   2  right medial  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast tissue with short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The specimen is inked black and the medial margin is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely from superior to inferior in K through O  Labeled   3  right superior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm portion of breast with a long suture designating the lateral  and a short suture designating the superior    anterior  margin  The specimen is inked black and the anterior flat surface    inferior aspect  is designated blue  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial and submitted in P through S  Labeled  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of fat from which multiple lymph nodes are dissected  The nodes are submitted in T through W  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Horace C  Wu  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST  SPECIMEN  1 PART B  RIGHT BREAST  SPECIMEN  2  MEDIAL  PART C  RIGHT BREAST  SPECIMEN  3  SUPERIOR  PART D  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   report_end  , Unchecked.
