cm anterior superior to this nodule is a third REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm indurated gray white nodule  likely biopsy site  which comes to 1 0cm of the posterior and 0 2cm of the anterior margin  Located 0 1cm posterior superior to the third nodule is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm indurated tan pink nodule  tumor  which comes to 0 1cm of the posterior and 0 9cm of the anterior margin  The remaining cut surface displays diffuse dense  nodular gray white fibrous tissue which has been previously blue dyed for a sentinel node mapping  Within the dense fibrous tissue is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm indurated area which comes to 0 1cm of the posterior margin and 2 0cm directly inferior from the first mass  Sectioning of the upper outer quadrant reveals no apparent gross lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   First mass  corresponds to fibroadenoma on microscopic examination    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Second mass  corresponds to fibroadenoma on microscopic examination    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Third and fourth masses  corresponds to tumor and biopsy site    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue between first mass and indurated area along the posterior aspect inferior to the first mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Indurated area along the posterior aspect inferior to first mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section from upper inner quadrant to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from upper outer quadrant which may represent lymph node  Received in formalin  labeled  right breast additional margin  superficial to mass    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm aggregate of tan red unremarkable fibrofatty tissue with no orientation  Sectioning reveals unremarkable tan yellow fibrofatty tissue  the specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1 AND  1A  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA I