Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 39 CLINICAL DATA  Left modified radical mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA IN 1 OF 22 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  2  BIOPSY CAVITY WITH FAT NECROSIS AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  3  FIBROCYSTIC DISEASE WITH ADENOSIS  CYSTS  FIBROSIS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  4  FOCAL MICROCALCIFICATION  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm left radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse containing a 1 0cm unremarkable nipple  2 0cm from the nipple is a 1 5cm well healed linear surgical scar  The axillary tail is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity  0 3cm from the nearest inked deep margin  The biopsy cavity is beneath the previously described surgical scar  in the medial inferior aspect of the specimen  The remaining breast parenchyma contains multiple cysts  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 3 0cm in greatest dimension  The cysts are filled with clear yellow to green fluid  The remaining breast parenchyma is firm  white  The axillary tail is dissected to reveal multiple rubbery  tan to pink lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0 8cm in greatest dimension  SECTION CODE  A I  axillary lymph nodes J M  representative sections of biopsy cavity and adjacent deep inked margin from medial to lateral N  sections just lateral to biopsy cavity O  representative section of cyst  at least 3 0cm away from biopsy cavity P  representative sections of nipple  Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
