Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma left breast at 3 o clock with DCIS positive at the anterior margin after re excision  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY WITH AXILLARY SAMPLING  1  FOCAL RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU ADJACENT TO HEALING BIOPSY SITE AND  0 2 CM FROM MARGINS  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 11 0cm unoriented left simple mastectomy specimen partially surfaced by a 25 7cm brown skin ellipse with an eccentric 7 5cm areola  Centrally within the areola is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm unremarkable nipple which comes to 5 5cm of the closest skin margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm curvilinear scar bordering the areola along the probable inferolateral aspect  Also noted is a second REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm healed linear scar also along the probable inferolateral aspect  The scars are REMOVED_DATE and 1 5cm of the closest probable inferolateral skin margin  Also noted along the probable upper outer aspect of the skin is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm pink brown papule which comes to 0 3cm of the skin margin  The anterior resection margin is inked blue and the posterior black  The specimen serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm hemorrhagic cavity surrounded by dense gray white fibrous tissue and yellow orange discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  The cavity comes to 3 0cm of the posterior margin and 2 8cm of the anterior margin  and is located in the probable lower outer quadrant  No other gross abnormalities are identified  Sectioning of the probable upper outer quadrant reveals several tan pink nodules up to 2 0cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity submitted from apparent medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Skin lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node each cassette  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY WITH AXILLARY SAMPLING  report_end  , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 14 CLINICAL DATA  80 year old female with breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE CELLULAR MUCINOUS CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of carcinoma  The tumor displays endocrine characteristics  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm simple mastectomy specimen containing a REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm unremarkable skin ellipse with an unremarkable centrally placed nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm firm  gritty  tan tissue mass that extends up to the overlying skin ellipse and to within 0 8cm of the nearest deep margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  No axillary tail is present  Section code  A  tumor with closest deep margin  representative section B  skin with tumor  representative section C F tumor  representative sections G  nipple  trisected  in entirety H  unremarkable parenchyma  representative sections Resident  FANG FANG  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  COMP  BREAST HEALTH CENTER REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Checked.
