ve result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 42 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tissue fragment with a 0 8cm firm lymph node  The node is sectioned to reveal a white tan  firm cut surface  Half the node is frozen as FX 1  and saved frozen  The remainder is submitted in cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  additional axillary nodes  right  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm aggregate of adipose tissue from which lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes B through C  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  right modified radical mastectomy   is a modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x 22 x 4 5cm  with an attached axilla of  14 x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0 cm and an overlying skin ellipse measuring  23 x 11cm   containing an eccentric nipple  4 0cm in diameter  7 7cm away from the medial end of the skin ellipse  The nipple areola complex is grossly unremarkable  No scars are grossly identified in the overlying skin ellipse  The deep resection margin consist of a smooth fascial plane  The specimen is inked black and the axillary contents are removed  A lymph node dissection is performed  The main mastectomy specimen is then serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm firm  gritty area with a stellate border tha