Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 46 CLINICAL DATA  Suture at short superior  long lateral                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY    INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  40    EXTENDING TO WITHIN LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED MARGIN  SLIDE D     DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  WITH COMEDO TYPE NECROSIS  60   EXTENDING TO AN INKED MARGIN  SLIDE I     ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA    FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  Overall  the tumor is approximately 2 0cm in greatest dimension and the infiltrating component is 1 1cm in greatest dimension  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends into the breast parenchyma at a distance from the infiltrating component  No lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 41 Consulting Pathologist s   Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                      HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Negative  progesterone receptor  Negative  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 57     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 26     DNA FLOW CYTOMETRY Addendum     DNA FLOW CYTOMETRY  BREAST   DNA DIPLOID  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The coefficients of variation of the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  peaks for two blocks are REMOVED_DATE and 6 9   The calculated  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  phase fractions are REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE  S phase fractions  REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  M fractions  REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE Added by  Thomas J  Flotte  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 41 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue containing two sutures  the short one designating the superior  and the long one designating the lateral edge  The superior portion is inked yellow  Sectioning reveals a 1 1cm in diameter irregular firm nodule with stellate tan yellow mottled appearance  0 1cm from the nearest 