Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  12 AUG 98 at 19 07 CLINICAL DATA  Right radical mastectomy 20 years ago  Now with left breast cancer  Status post biopsy  Short suture superior  long suture lateral with attached axillary tail                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWENTY EIGHT OF TWENTY EIGHT LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  18 AUG 98 at 17 38                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left Breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm left modified radial mastectomy specimen with attached axillary tail  There is a short suture designating the superior margin and a long suture designating the lateral margin  The specimen is surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 9 5cm white skin ellipse with a central  flattened nipple areolar complex  There is a 5 0cm linear sutured  healing incision 5 0cm superolaterally from the nipple  The entire specimen is inked black  Serial sectioning beneath the aforementioned scar reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm hemorrhagic biopsy cavity filled with liquid blood  as well as clot  The parenchyma surrounding the biopsy cavity is focally indurated with adjacent  bright yellow parenchymal changes  The biopsy cavity is located 1 2cm from the closest deep margin  5 5cm from the closest superior margin  2 0cm from the closest medial margin  7 5cm from the closest lateral margin  and 9 5cm from the closest inferior margin  The remainder of the specimen is composed predominantly of fatty tissue interspersed with dense  white