0 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm firm  tan to yellow piece of fibroadipose tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm white  hard  stellate area  A representative section from this area is frozen as FX 1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the specimen is submitted entirely in A through L  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  Ross Charles Wheeler  M D  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
