Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 MAY 95 ACCESSIONED ON  31 MAY 95 at 16 01 CLINICAL DATA  Excision of carcinoma of the breast two weeks ago at MGH                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  1  RESIDUAL INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  25    AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM MEASURED FROM TISSUE SECTIONS  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE 2  RESIDUAL INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  75    CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES  3  BIOPSY CAVITY  WITH SURROUNDING FAT NECROSIS  FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL RESPONSE AND FIBROSIS  4  CUTANEOUS SCAR  NOTE  Intraductal carcinoma  but not infiltrating carcinoma  is present at several inked surfaces  Skeletal muscle at the deep aspect of the re excision is free of tumor  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  Tumor infiltrating lymphocytes are scant  Fibrocystic changes and a hyalinized small duct papilloma are also present  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY  EXCISION  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 25 LYMPH NODES  POSITIVE NODE REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIAMETER  WITHOUT EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION   Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 04                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast re excision   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm left re excision lumpectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm skin ellipse  that contains a 2 5cm linear healed skin incision  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm biopsy cavity that is partially filled with tan  fibrous tissue admixed with blood and surrounded by tan to white fibrotic breast parenchyma  The biopsy cavity extends from 0 5cm below the overlying skin ellipse to abut the deep resection margin at its closest extent  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan white fibrous area adjacent to the biopsy cavity at one edge  that extends to abut the closest deep margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is tan yellow and grossly unremarkable  B SECTION CODE  A C  biopsy cavity  closest deep margin D  fibrous area adjacent to biopsy cavity  closest deep E F  biopsy cavity G H  representative section of biopsy cavity overlying skin I J  en face sections of edges of lumpectomy  grossly unremarkable breast  Received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm segment of fat containing multiple tan lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 3 0cm in diameter  The largest node has a tan pink nodule cut surface  Nodes are submitted in cassettes K through Q  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  Simon Bergman  M D  PART A  AXILLARY NODES  LEFT  PART B  BREAST RE EXCISION  LEFT  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 01 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive carcinoma grade 3 with  margin                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY CAVITY AND REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEVERAL FOCI  ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY CAVITY  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Lymphatic vessel and blood vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 14                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 36 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm simple mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm skin ellipse and unremarkable nipple areolar complex  There is a suture designating the superior aspect  There is a 7 0cm horizontal  linear  well healed scar present 4 5cm superior to the nipple  The excised surface is inked black  with the anterior surface overinked red  Cross sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm biopsy cavity 1 0cm beneath the skin  beneath the scar  and abutting the deep margin along a broad front  The biopsy cavity is lined by white fibrous tissue with a few fibrous strands extending into the adjacent fat  There is also fat necrosis surrounding the biopsy cavity site  Tissue away from the biopsy cavity is mixed white fibrous parenchyma and fatty tissue  No discrete lesions are identified  Section code  A  Biopsy cavity with deep margin B F  Sections of biopsy cavity from inferior to superior G H  Representative sections of tissue away from biopsy cavity  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Checked.
