ATE x 0 4cm hard nodule which is 4 5cm from the posterior resection margin  Also noted in the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm tan red  granular  and firm area in the 1 o clock portion of the breast  This area is 3 5cm from the posterior margin and 3 1cm from the anterior skin  The surrounding uninvolved breast parenchyma is predominantly yellow  lobulated  and fatty with focal areas of more tan white and firm fibrous tissue  The lateral portion of the specimen is explored and no lymph nodes are present  Representative sections are submitted as per section code  Section Code  B E U Y  Representative sections of 10 o clock area  F  Closest posterior margin to 10 o clock area  G  10 o clock area to nearest anterior margin  H K  Z DD  Firm 1 o clock area  L  Closest posterior margin to 1 o clock area  M P  Medial breast  Q  Hard 0 5cm nodule inferior to the 10 o clock area  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional right axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fragment of yellow fibrofatty tissue containing scattered small lymph nodes  All individual lymph nodes present in the specimen are submitted into cassette R  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  axillary skin tag  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm polypoid fragment of tan and wrinkled skin which is bisected and entirely submitted into cassette S  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  inframammary skin tag  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of tan and wrinkled polypoid skin which is bisected and entirely submitted into cassette T  Resident  PAUL MICHAELS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  STEWART M  KNOEPP  MD   Ph D  O R  Diagnosis by  William C  Faquin MD PhD                          