ectioned to reveal diffuse dense gray white fibrous tissue with marked cystic change  These cysts are up to 2 1cm in greatest dimension  Sectioning the upper outer quadrant reveals several possible tan red lymph nodes up to 0 7cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and tissue from the upper outer quadrant  which may represent lymph nodes is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE  NEGATIVE NODE  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE  NEGATIVE NODE  Fellow Review by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Joshua Kish M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of 