Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 01 CLINICAL DATA                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  95    INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  5    NOTE  The margins appear free of carcinoma  but focally the tumor approaches close to the margin  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  A minor component of the lesion has a tubular pattern  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 18 17                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 16     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast mass  is a 2 x 2 x 1cm fibrofatty piece of tissue with a needle localization wire  The external surface is inked and sectioning reveals a firm  poorly defined  gray white tumor  measuring 0 8cm in greatest diameter  A small piece of tissue is taken as frozen section  1 and the block is kept frozen  The remainder of the tissue is submitted in cassettes A E  Gross Description by  C  Diana Jordan  MD Resident  David Andrews  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST   LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
