Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Signed Out by  John H Eichhorn  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer  Simple mastectomy  Stitch   12 00 FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 2 TO 3  SCATTERED FOCI ADJACENT TO THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF STROMAL OR LYMPHATIC INVASION  MARGINS NEGATIVE FOR TUMOR  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  Byron  REMOVE_MRN and  right breast   is a 25 x 20 x 2 5 cm oriented right simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating 12 o clock position  The overlying tan brown skin ellipse measures 22 x 10 5cm and contains a 3 x 3 cm areola and a 1 x 1 x 0 3 cm nipple  both of which are grossly unremarkable  There is a 10 cm linear  well healed scar present between 7 and 10 o clock  4 5cm from the areola  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  There is a 9 x 5 5 cm exposed cavity on the posterior surface in the outer quadrant which lies beneath the well healed scar on the overlying skin  The cavity is lined by a tan pink  smooth and glistening lining and contains a metallic clip  The cavity is exposed on the posterior surface and lies 3 5cm from the anterior surface  The breast parenchyma adjacent to the cavity shows focal fat necrosis  The rest of the breast parenchyma in the mid and inner quadrant shows tan yellow  lobulated fibroadipose tissue  No other discrete mass or lesion is identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   